### High-Level Overview

This Python script initializes an `aiohttp.ClientSession` object, which is used for making asynchronous HTTP requests. The session is stored in a global variable named `session`, which allows it to be reused throughout the application without needing to recreate it each time a request is made. This approach helps in maintaining connection pooling and other optimizations provided by `aiohttp`.

### Global Variables

- **session**: An optional `aiohttp.ClientSession` object. It is initialized once at the start of the application and reused for all subsequent HTTP requests. If no session is created, it remains `None`.

