This Python script is designed to interact with an IO Expander board, specifically focusing on controlling an RGB LED using a potentiometer. The script uses the `ioexpander` library to communicate with the hardware and the `colorama` library for colored logging output.

### High-Level Overview
The main class, `Potentiometer`, encapsulates the functionality required to read the position of a potentiometer and use it to control an RGB LED. It reads an analog input from the potentiometer, scales this value to a user-defined range, and then maps this scaled value to an RGB color which is applied to the LED.

