# Linear Chain of Reactions Simulation

This Python script simulates a linear chain of chemical reactions using the Tellurium library. The model represents a series of enzymatic reactions where each species is converted into the next in a sequential manner. The simulation aims to understand the dynamics of these reactions over time.

## Classes and Structs

### No Classes or Structs Defined

The provided source code does not define any classes or structs. All functionality is encapsulated within the main script.

## Global Variables and Standalone Functions

### Global Variables

- `model`: A string containing the SBML model definition for the linear chain of reactions.
- `r`: An instance of the `RoadRunner` class from the Tellurium library, which is used to load and simulate the model.
- `result`: A NumPy array containing the simulation results.
- `plotWithLegend`: A method of the `RoadRunner` class used to plot the simulation results with legends.

### Standalone Functions

- `te.loada(model)`: Loads the model defined in the `model` string into a `RoadRunner` object.
- `r.simulate(start_time, end_time, num_points)`: Simulates the model from `start_time` to `end_time` with
