The provided Python script defines a function `add_losses` that processes a spectrum by deriving potential loss ions based on the precursor mass. The function takes an input spectrum and optional parameters to specify the range of m/z values for the derived losses. It then calculates the m/z values and intensities of these losses and adds them to the spectrum object.

## Classes and Structs

### Fragments

